# Claim Preservation Profile v0.1.0 — integrity manifest
#
# WHAT THIS MANIFEST RECORDS
#   The exact bytes of the two normative v0.1 artifacts in the v0.1.0 release.
#   It records those bytes; it does not freeze future versions. Verify with:
#       cd spec/v0.1 && sha256sum -c CHECKSUMS.sha256
#
# WHAT THIS DOES NOT FREEZE, CLAIM, OR ESTABLISH
#   - A versioned release is NOT a standard and does not freeze future versions.
#     The profile remains EXPERIMENTAL and may change without a compatibility
#     guarantee.
#   - Integrity is not truth (CPP-8). A matching digest establishes that these
#     bytes are the bytes recorded here. It establishes nothing about whether the
#     profile is correct, complete, sound, reviewed, or fit for any purpose.
#   - This manifest covers only the two files named below. It does not cover the
#     conformance fixtures, the fixture schemas, the validator, the tests, or any
#     repository document. Those change independently and are not pinned here.
#   - The manifest is unsigned. It carries no key attribution and no timestamp
#     authority, so it cannot establish who produced it or when.
#   - It says nothing about any other version of the profile, past or future.
#
